    "result_text": "Done. The test suite is green.\n\nI extended the business-day rule to skip public holidays by editing only `BusinessDays.java`:\n\n- Added a private `HOLIDAYS` set with the five fixed dates (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28).\n- Rewrote `rollForward` as a simple loop that advances one day while the date isn't a business day \u2014 matching the acceptance test's day-by-day roll semantics, so a weekend that lands on a holiday (or consecutive holidays) keeps rolling.\n- Extracted the weekend/holiday check into a small private `isBusinessDay` helper.\n\nStructural impact stayed minimal: a single file touched, `rollForward` kept at CC 2, and the new logic lives in a tiny cohesive helper rather than growing an existing complex method. The two call sites (`Owner.setRegistrationDate` and `DailyRegistrations`) were left untouched and inherit the new behavior through the same `rollForward` entry point.",
